                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e55ffb4b-0fc6-31a6-ade5-a4756f451deb",
                        "entry_id": "b0d2416e-44af-3eea-b6ed-8cd16f7332fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "wrok,wraakzucht"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7269f4db-6422-4348-ba4a-999f1d6bd792",
                                "sense_id": "e55ffb4b-0fc6-31a6-ade5-a4756f451deb",
                                "text": "Niet eerder in de afgelopen halve eeuw is het gevaar van een nieuwe wereldoorlog zo groot geweest. En nooit eerder heeft het Westen er zo beroerd voor gestaan. Het huidige Rusland vormt een veel grotere bedreiging dan de Sovjet-Unie tijdens Chroestjov of Brezjnev ooit is geweest. Poetin wordt gedreven door rancune over de teloorgang van Rusland als supermacht, wil de EU vernietigen en zal niet rusten voor hij zijn Rijk weer tot aan de Oder heeft hersteld, met alle geweld..."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "74c0b2e2-7607-4eb6-9489-a9ee029e245c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0d2416e-44af-3eea-b6ed-8cd16f7332fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "e55ffb4b-0fc6-31a6-ade5-a4756f451deb",
                        "target_lang_word": "grudge",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grudge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                        "entry_id": "9766cfca-e185-32ba-b5ef-8a977b003290",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Deep-seated and/or long-term animosity or ill will about something or someone, especially due to perceived mistreatment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e987760-2eaa-42e9-9b98-8044b434ea0b",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "to have, hold, or bear a grudge against someone"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c090044-e9c2-4a14-9c82-08bf500b4ce0",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "Bag. And if I do not my good Lord damme me for it\nI haue an old grudge at him cole black curre,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "951fa6de-29be-43e7-b901-771a1cd8d47f",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "I have never mentioned it to a human creature; I have kept my grudge to myself. I daresay I have been wicked, but my grudge has grown old with me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51367910-6868-4bed-881a-98367103d71c",
                                                "sense_id": "7e3abd29-e9db-38c5-adda-111fbe54a0e3",
                                                "text": "It is towards Saduko that he bears a grudge, for you know, my father, one should never pull a drowning man out of the stream — which is what Saduko did, for had it not been for his treachery, Cetewayo would have sunk beneath the water of Death — especially if it is only to spite a woman who hates him."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "grudge",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                        "entry_id": "32cbaa5b-4430-3b1e-9d7c-125eea328908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be unwilling to give or allow (someone something)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5fd433a-08ae-4932-832d-e8304f2e0058",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "Wee shall finde our whole life so necessarily ioyned with sorrow, that we ought rather delight (and take pleasure) in Gods louing chastisements, and admonitions, then any way murmure and grudge at our crosses, or tribulations :"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5428323f-3106-4c32-b8c1-8f6c6742c7ec",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "If we of the central land were to grudge you what is beneficial, and not to compassionate your wants, then wherewithal could you foreigners manage to exist?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "337e4377-d692-4629-abed-e2fa58423c6c",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "Of course, his interest in the war and in the regiment was unbounded; he did not take to drill with especial readiness, but he was insatiable of it, and grudged every moment of relaxation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49474be3-bc5c-473a-b12e-024aa688b90d",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "Our two inimitable drolls did a roaring trade with their broadsheets among lovers of the comedy element and nobody who has a corner in his heart for real Irish fun without vulgarity will grudge them their hardearned pennies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11bddf93-c2bb-4b3c-b7c2-f7c1681148d3",
                                                "sense_id": "bb34a84c-9a31-338b-a8fa-1379133bbe0d",
                                                "text": "I've never seen such people for borrowing and lending; there was dough changing hands in all directions, and nobody grudged anyone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c7023b27-4ed8-36f9-bd92-5233688a4c4e",
                                        "entry_id": "32cbaa5b-4430-3b1e-9d7c-125eea328908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grumble, complain; to be dissatisfied."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f86e484b-f3b1-4050-aa25-0bb481bc9435",
                                                "sense_id": "c7023b27-4ed8-36f9-bd92-5233688a4c4e",
                                                "text": "And the pharises, and scribes grudged sainge: He receaveth to his company synners [...]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c314939f-e89d-32b2-89c2-663f458d1ff6",
                                        "entry_id": "32cbaa5b-4430-3b1e-9d7c-125eea328908",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hold or harbour with malicious disposition or purpose; to cherish enviously."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "784a5f1a-922c-4884-91ed-24242584a738",
                                                "sense_id": "c314939f-e89d-32b2-89c2-663f458d1ff6",
                                                "text": "Perish they / That grudge one thought against your majesty!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d4492629-f630-4564-a35f-8d7f57595cc5",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0d2416e-44af-3eea-b6ed-8cd16f7332fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "e55ffb4b-0fc6-31a6-ade5-a4756f451deb",
                        "target_lang_word": "rancour",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rancour",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f42a93e2-f9d4-3d90-9410-9a99d4668035",
                                        "entry_id": "0fa5f30c-1d92-3930-b16d-b7df0a6ed27a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "British, Canada, and Australia spelling of rancor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "119b9d55-e99d-4b61-899e-738f75aa45cb",
                                                "sense_id": "f42a93e2-f9d4-3d90-9410-9a99d4668035",
                                                "text": "By some paradoxical evolution rancour and intolerance have been established in the vanguard of primitive Christianity. Mrs. Spoker, in common with many of the stricter disciples of righteousness, was as inclement in demeanour as she was cadaverous in aspect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c068df6-1c58-4e84-9a04-99a56c3b0e98",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0d2416e-44af-3eea-b6ed-8cd16f7332fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "e55ffb4b-0fc6-31a6-ade5-a4756f451deb",
                        "target_lang_word": "resentment",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "resentment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "559c33d6-523b-36c4-8012-e9f9f40336be",
                                        "entry_id": "246d733f-e844-3bed-adc0-560e770bfc77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anger or displeasure stemming from belief that one or one's group has been wronged or betrayed by others; indignation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9a9661d-3dc7-40e7-9bfc-db59cea1f77f",
                                                "sense_id": "559c33d6-523b-36c4-8012-e9f9f40336be",
                                                "text": "Amongst the most violent against him was Mrs. Bennet, whose dislike of his general behaviour, was sharpened into particular resentment, by his having slighted one of her daughters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62cd1bfe-1381-45e2-ba99-93fa5666badf",
                                                "sense_id": "559c33d6-523b-36c4-8012-e9f9f40336be",
                                                "text": "Younger [Customs] examiners, who, perhaps, have not yet acquired the intuition resulting from years of experience, seem partly responsible for the closer examination of incoming luggage. Not only is this closer scrutiny arousing feelings of resentment among passengers, but it is causing serious delays in the departure of boat trains, many of which have been reaching their destinations two or three hours late."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b755a0a0-de25-494e-81f0-2e36f71556e7",
                                                "sense_id": "559c33d6-523b-36c4-8012-e9f9f40336be",
                                                "text": "“I Love Lisa” opens with one of my favorite underappreciated running jokes from The Simpsons: the passive-aggressive, quietly contentious relationship of radio jocks Bill and Marty, whose mindless happy talk regularly gives way to charged exchanges that betray the simmering resentment and disappointment perpetually lingering just under the surface of their relationship."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac710696-84ae-3fbb-bd4b-6c2b1683980e",
                                        "entry_id": "246d733f-e844-3bed-adc0-560e770bfc77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of holding something in the mind as a subject of contemplation, or of being inclined to reflect upon it; feeling; impression."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8719a194-3dd3-4238-85ee-c5138ef6ff04",
                                                "sense_id": "ac710696-84ae-3fbb-bd4b-6c2b1683980e",
                                                "text": "It is a greater wonder that so many of them die, with so little resentment of their danger."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8550876f-7dd2-4ce3-a34f-b12e9dda425d",
                                                "sense_id": "ac710696-84ae-3fbb-bd4b-6c2b1683980e",
                                                "text": "In my mind it is a ſign of a great deal of natural Integrity and inbred Nobleneſs of ſpirit, that maugre [in spite of] the heavineſs of his Complexion that thus ſtrongly bears him dovvn from apprehending ſo concerning Metaphyſicall Truths, yet he retains ſo vivid reſentments of the more sſolid Morality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "093c1bab-6c73-3005-bebc-95e759258cc6",
                                        "entry_id": "246d733f-e844-3bed-adc0-560e770bfc77",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Satisfaction; gratitude."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2bf52af-0def-420e-aa49-6d0c721fb36b",
                                                "sense_id": "093c1bab-6c73-3005-bebc-95e759258cc6",
                                                "text": "The Council taking notice of the many good services performed by Mr. John Milton […] have thought fit to declare their resentment and good acceptance of the same."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "35b8c8d0-d258-4c2e-9b93-ffd083840670",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0d2416e-44af-3eea-b6ed-8cd16f7332fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "e55ffb4b-0fc6-31a6-ade5-a4756f451deb",
